{"id":"n-20261029-4zbozi","category":"tech","display_title":"Apple Debuts Touchscreen MacBook Pro Lineup","display_title_he":"אפל משיקה סדרת MacBook Pro עם מסך מגע","short_summary":"Apple has introduced its first touchscreen MacBook Pro, alongside a top-tier configuration option reaching an unprecedented price of $14,549. The launch reflects shifting hardware design choices amid ongoing industry memory shortages.","english_level":"C1","words":493,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"TechCrunch","domain":"techcrunch.com","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/28/apples-touchscreen-macbook-pro-pushes-laptop-pricing-to-a-new-extreme","title":"Apple’s touchscreen MacBook Pro pushes laptop pricing to a new extreme","published_at":"2026-10-28T22:47:50.000Z"},{"name":"The Verge","domain":"theverge.com","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1021308/apple-touchscreen-macbook-pro-proled-xdr-fully-specced","title":"Apple charges $14,549 for a fully specced touchscreen MacBook Pro","published_at":"2026-10-28T20:12:44.000Z"},{"name":"Wired","domain":"wired.com","url":"https://www.wired.com/story/m6-macbook-pro-price-problem","title":"The New M6 MacBook Pro Has a Serious Price Problem","published_at":"2026-10-28T18:57:22.000Z"},{"name":"Ars Technica","domain":"arstechnica.com","url":"https://arstechnica.com/apple/2026/10/touchscreen-macbook-pro-hands-on-oled-looks-great-on-a-mac","title":"Touchscreen MacBook Pro hands-on: OLED looks great on a Mac","published_at":"2026-10-28T19:10:29.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-28T18:57:22.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-29T07:10:54.314Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Apple has officially introduced its first touchscreen MacBook Pro models, signaling a major strategic evolution nearly a decade after the tech giant initially experimented with interactive laptop controls via the Touch Bar. Abandoning its previous resistance to full touchscreen integration on laptops, the company unveiled a revamped hardware lineup that blends high-end performance with interactive displays. However, this long-anticipated innovation arrives alongside unprecedented pricing structures. The baseline 14-inch touchscreen model begins at $2,899, while the 16-inch base model starts at $3,399, positioning the new family at the premium end of an already expensive consumer electronics landscape. Preorders officially open on October 30, with store arrival scheduled for November 6.","While base prices are steep, maximizing the internal hardware configuration drives costs into extraordinary territory. According to initial listings from Apple’s online configurator, a fully specced 14-inch model reaches $14,249, whereas the top-of-the-line 16-inch iteration hits $14,549. Both maximum configurations are powered by Apple's highest-tier M5 Max processor, featuring an 18-core CPU and a 40-core GPU. To reach these top price points, buyers must select 128GB of unified memory—which alone adds $2,000—alongside a nano-texture glass screen finish for an additional $150. These specs cater to professional creators demanding extreme computational power and anti-reflective display performance.","The primary factor driving these astronomical prices is Apple's new top-tier storage option. Choosing a 16TB solid-state drive adds a staggering $7,000 to the purchase price. Lower storage tiers remain costly as well; upgrading to a 4TB SSD costs $1,000 extra, while selecting an 8TB drive adds $3,000, bringing the fully equipped 16-inch model without max storage to $10,549. Technology analysts attribute these escalating prices to a combination of an ongoing global memory shortage and the tech industry's immense, surging hardware demand driven by artificial intelligence development. To put this pricing in perspective, the maximum configuration for the previous 16-inch MacBook Pro topped out at $10,149, meaning the new flagship configuration raises the ceiling by $4,400.","Alongside its flagship touchscreen launch, Apple also refreshed its entry-level 14-inch MacBook Pro with the newly released M6 processor. Priced at $1,999 for 16GB of memory and 512GB of storage, this model incorporates a $300 price increase introduced across the Mac lineup earlier this year. The M6 silicon features enhanced graphics performance and a dual Neural Engine tailored specifically to accelerate AI tasks within creative software applications. Despite these performance gains, product reviewers note that the steep entry price creates an intriguing dilemma for budget-conscious buyers exploring alternative setups.","For instance, industry commentators point out that the current market price of an M6 Mac Mini combined with an M5 MacBook Air equals the single $1,999 purchase price of the base M6 MacBook Pro. While buyers choosing that dual-device combination miss out on the MacBook Pro's vibrant Mini-LED display and superior speakers, they gain immense flexibility—particularly as more users deploy compact desktop machines as always-on AI servers controlled remotely. Alternatively, buyers can spend just $200 more to secure an M5 Pro chip inside the same chassis, raising questions about where the best value lies in Apple's current laptop portfolio."],"facts":[{"fact":"Apple officially announced touchscreen MacBook Pro models starting at $2,899 for the 14-inch and $3,399 for the 16-inch base models.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"A fully configured touchscreen MacBook Pro costs up to $14,249 for the 14-inch and $14,549 for the 16-inch model, which is $4,400 more than the previous top-spec model.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The maximum configuration includes an M5 Max chip with an 18-core CPU and 40-core GPU, 128GB of RAM ($2,000), nano-texture glass ($150), and a new 16TB SSD option that costs $7,000 alone.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Preorders for the touchscreen MacBook Pro open on October 30, with store availability beginning on November 6.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ongoing global memory shortages and high demand for AI hardware contribute to the steep pricing pressure.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Apple also refreshed its standard 14-inch MacBook Pro with the M6 chip starting at $1,999 for 16GB RAM and 512GB SSD, following an earlier $300 price hike across the lineup.","sources":[3]},{"fact":"The M6 processor features improved graphics performance and a dual Neural Engine to speed up creative AI workflows.","sources":[3]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Apple","lemma":"Apple","pos":"name","he":"אפל (חברת טכנולוגיה)","name":true},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן רשמי","name":false},{"text":"introduced","lemma":"introduce","pos":"verb","he":"הציגה, הדיקה לראשונה","name":false},{"text":"touchscreen","lemma":"touchscreen","pos":"noun","he":"מסך מגע","name":false},{"text":"MacBook Pro","lemma":"MacBook Pro","pos":"name","he":"מקבוק פרו (סדרת מחשבים ניידים של אפל)","name":true},{"text":"models","lemma":"model","pos":"noun","he":"דגמים","name":false},{"text":"signaling","lemma":"signal","pos":"verb","he":"מסמנת, מורה על","name":false},{"text":"strategic","lemma":"strategic","pos":"adjective","he":"אסטרטגי","name":false},{"text":"evolution","lemma":"evolution","pos":"noun","he":"התפתחות, אבולוציה","name":false},{"text":"decade","lemma":"decade","pos":"noun","he":"עשור","name":false},{"text":"tech giant","lemma":"tech giant","pos":"compound","he":"ענקית טכנולוגיה","name":false},{"text":"initially","lemma":"initially","pos":"adverb","he":"בתחילה","name":false},{"text":"experimented","lemma":"experiment","pos":"verb","he":"נסתה, התנסתה","name":false},{"text":"interactive","lemma":"interactive","pos":"adjective","he":"אינטראקטיבי, אינטראקטיביים","name":false},{"text":"controls","lemma":"control","pos":"noun","he":"בקרים, אמצעי שליטה","name":false},{"text":"Touch Bar","lemma":"Touch Bar","pos":"name","he":"טאץ' בר (פס מגע במחשבי מקבוק בעבר)","name":true},{"text":"Abandoning","lemma":"abandon","pos":"ver